# The build context is the compose project directory, and on the NAS that is the
# same directory the database and the thumbnails live in: docker-compose.yml mounts
# /vol1/docker/tuping/data into /data, and TUPING_THUMBS points at thumbs/ inside
# it. Without this file every 构建 in the fnOS Docker panel packs the whole SQLite
# database and thumbnail cache and ships it to the Docker daemon, so that the
# Dockerfile can COPY one 15 MB binary. None of it can reach the image, which copies
# exactly one file, so ignoring it only removes work.
#
# The two entries that matter are data/ and thumbs/; the rest is hygiene for a
# directory a deployer also browses with the file manager.

data/
thumbs/
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm

.git
.gitignore
*.log
.env

# The files the build itself reads are not context either.
Dockerfile
docker-compose.yml
.dockerignore
README.md
